Closing straight into an incoming charge is risky, but changing course now is fatal. I sprint forward, attempting to outpace his swing and disarm him before he recovers.

Charging straight into an axe cleave without the requisite speed is suicide. I fail to slip inside his reach. The heavy steel blade crashes down across my chest, cutting through flesh and bone in a single devastating strike.

}
