#if(v_agility >= 2 && v_b2_ch5_scimitar != 0) {
 

The gladiator closes the distance and plants his boots a dozen feet away, sizing me up with a smug, heavy grin. He says nothing. The arrogance in his stance says everything—he sees an easy slaughter.

The horn sounds. The man lunges forward, hoisting the heavy battleaxe high for an overhead cleave.

Meeting an axe rush head-on leaves no margin for error, but there is no time to rethink the plan. I sprint forward, moving fast enough to slip under his guard before his arms come down.

The burst of speed catches him flat-footed. I drive the point of the scimitar between his ribs. The curved blade prevents a deep puncture, but the sharp bite of steel is enough to send him staggering back in panic. I press the opening, sweeping the blade in a low cut that takes his footing. He tumbles onto his back, the battleaxe slipping from his fingers. I kick the weapon across the sand and press my scimitar to his jugular.

}
