Meeting an axe rush head-on leaves no margin for error, but there is no time to rethink the plan. I sprint forward, moving fast enough to slip under his guard before his arms come down.

The burst of speed catches him flat-footed. I drive my dagger into his exposed left flank, finding the soft gap beneath his leather harness. The puncture bites deep enough to send him recoiling in terror. I follow the stagger instantly, slashing across his center of gravity. He loses his footing and crashes onto his back, the axe falling from his grasp. I boot the weapon away and pin my dagger to his throat.

}
