ID: B2-Ch05b-Tactic3
TEXT:

set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_b2_ch5_scimitar == 0 && v_reflexes >= 2 && v_strength >= 2 || v_reflexes >= 2 && v_strength >= 1 && v_b2_ch5_scimitar != 0)
set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_b2_ch5_scimitar == 0 && v_strength < 2 || v_strength == 0 && v_b2_ch5_scimitar != 0 || v_reflexes < 2)
#if(v_reflexes >= 2 && v_strength >= 1 && v_b2_ch5_scimitar != 0) {
 

The gladiator closes the distance and plants his boots a dozen feet away, sizing me up with a smug, heavy grin. He says nothing. The arrogance in his stance says everything—he sees an easy slaughter.

The horn sounds. The man lunges forward, hoisting the heavy battleaxe high for an overhead cleave.

I hold my ground, watching his shoulders to read the swing, waiting for the exact split second to strip his weapon.

Dodging a two-handed battleaxe wielded by a seasoned pit fighter demands total focus. The wide swings whistle past my face, churning the sand, each blow carrying enough weight to shear through a wooden post. The extra length of the scimitar gives me room to maneuver, parrying the closest sweeps.

The moment he overcommits on a downward chop, his balance breaks. I hook the scimitar's curved tip around the axe head and wrench with boosted strength. The weapon tears free from his hands, flying across the dirt.

I step in before he can recover. He scrambles back, trips over his own heels, and falls flat on his back. My scimitar point pins him to the ground at the throat.

}
#if(v_b2_ch5_scimitar == 0 && v_reflexes >= 2 && v_strength >= 2) {
 

The gladiator closes the distance and plants his boots a dozen feet away, sizing me up with a smug, heavy grin. He says nothing. The arrogance in his stance says everything—he sees an easy slaughter.

The horn sounds. The man lunges forward, hoisting the heavy battleaxe high for an overhead cleave.

I hold my ground, watching his shoulders to read the swing, waiting for the exact split second to strip his weapon.

Dodging a two-handed battleaxe wielded by a seasoned pit fighter demands total focus. The wide swings whistle past my face, churning the sand, each blow carrying enough weight to shear through a wooden post. My heightened reflexes keep me a fraction of an inch ahead of every whistling edge.

I let him wear himself out with three furious swings. On the fourth, his recovery lags. I step inside his extended guard and slash my dagger hard against the axe haft with full strength. The violent shock breaks his grip, sending the axe clattering away.

I surge forward. The man scrambles backward, loses his footing in the sand, and hits the ground hard. I drop my dagger tip right against his throat.

}
#if(v_reflexes < 2) {
 

The gladiator closes the distance and plants his boots a dozen feet away, sizing me up with a smug, heavy grin. He says nothing. The arrogance in his stance says everything—he sees an easy slaughter.

The horn sounds. The man lunges forward, hoisting the heavy battleaxe high for an overhead cleave.

I hold my ground, watching his shoulders to read the swing, waiting for the exact split second to strip his weapon.

Dodging a two-handed battleaxe wielded by a seasoned pit fighter demands total focus.

My unenhanced reflexes cannot keep pace with the massive reach of his swings. The first horizontal slash comes around faster than I can track, catching me full across the ribs and cutting me down where I stand.

}
#if(v_strength == 0 && v_reflexes >= 2 && v_b2_ch5_scimitar != 0) {
 

The gladiator closes the distance and plants his boots a dozen feet away, sizing me up with a smug, heavy grin. He says nothing. The arrogance in his stance says everything—he sees an easy slaughter.

The horn sounds. The man lunges forward, hoisting the heavy battleaxe high for an overhead cleave.

I hold my ground, watching his shoulders to read the swing, waiting for the exact split second to strip his weapon.

Dodging a two-handed battleaxe wielded by a seasoned pit fighter demands total focus. The wide swings whistle past my face, churning the sand, each blow carrying enough weight to shear through a wooden post. The extra length of the scimitar gives me room to maneuver, parrying the closest sweeps.

The moment he overcommits on a downward chop, his balance breaks. I hook the scimitar's curved tip around the axe head and pull, but without sufficient muscle, his two-handed grip holds firm. The failed wrench stalls my footing. In the heartbeat I lose, the warrior whips the axe around and cleaves straight through my chest.

}
#if(v_b2_ch5_scimitar == 0 && v_reflexes >= 2 && v_strength < 2) {
 

The gladiator closes the distance and plants his boots a dozen feet away, sizing me up with a smug, heavy grin. He says nothing. The arrogance in his stance says everything—he sees an easy slaughter.

The horn sounds. The man lunges forward, hoisting the heavy battleaxe high for an overhead cleave.

I hold my ground, watching his shoulders to read the swing, waiting for the exact split second to strip his weapon.

Dodging a two-handed battleaxe wielded by a seasoned pit fighter demands total focus. The wide swings whistle past my face, churning the sand, each blow carrying enough weight to shear through a wooden post. My heightened reflexes keep me a fraction of an inch ahead of every whistling edge.

I let him wear himself out with three furious swings. On the fourth, his recovery lags. I step inside his extended guard and slash my dagger hard against the axe haft, but without enough strength behind the blow, the wood barely budges in his grip. The recoil kills my momentum. In the split second I freeze, his backswing takes my head.

}
