I dance around his swings until his stance slips, then lunge in to drive my dagger into his chest. But my angle is too predictable. Even off balance, the veteran snaps his axe handle upward, blocking the thrust and smashing the heavy wooden haft across my temple. My vision blurs. In that dazed second, the battleaxe comes down and ends the fight.

