ID: B2-Ch05b-Caliber
TEXT:

set(v_ac_b2_ch5_united,1) if (v_b2_ch5_spare == 1 && v_b2_ch5_wilhelm == 1)
achievement("United we stand",v_ac_b2_ch5_united)
#if(v_b2_ch5_spare == 0) {
 "Very well," the announcer says, waving a hand in resignation. "Are there any further volunteers wishing to join the undesirable ranks?"

The remaining gladiators stand in dead silence. No one else moves.

"Splendid," the announcer calls out. "Let us commence the final contest! Volunteers for the hunt, step forward!"

One swordsman takes a hesitant step onto the sand, but a burly fighter behind him grabs his collar and yanks him backward.

"Are you eager to meet your ancestors?" the second fighter mutters under his breath. "Look at who is standing on that sand! The dwarf smashed through manticores and scorpions with his bare hands. The armored healer took on an entire wave of monsters without a scratch on his plate. You have to be insane to charge those people!"

The murmur spreads through the ranks. The few gladiators who had considered volunteering now shift on their heels, eyeing our line with growing dread.

}
#if(v_b2_ch5_spare == 1) {
 "Very well," the announcer says, waving a hand in resignation. "Are there any further volunteers wishing to join the undesirable ranks?"

"I do!"

The axe fighter I spared in the previous duel limps forward, his wounded thigh heavily bandaged. He takes his place at the end of our line.

"I do not leave this coliseum while carrying an unpaid life debt from the sands," he says firmly.

"Fine, fine," the announcer groans, rubbing his temples. "Anyone else?"

The gladiators stand in dead silence.

"At last," the announcer calls out. "Let us commence the final contest! Volunteers for the hunt, step forward!"

One swordsman takes a hesitant step onto the sand, but a burly fighter behind him grabs his collar and yanks him backward.

"Are you eager to meet your ancestors?" the second fighter mutters under his breath. "Look at who is standing on that sand! The dwarf smashed through manticores and scorpions with his bare hands. The armored healer took on an entire wave of monsters without a scratch on his plate. You have to be insane to charge those people!"

The murmur spreads through the ranks. The few gladiators who had considered volunteering now shift on their heels, eyeing our line with growing dread.

}
"Truly?" the announcer cries out in disbelief. "Not a single soul? Do you understand what the crown offers for the heads of these outcasts? Full pardons on the spot! Chests of gold bullion!"

"Better poor on two feet than wealthy in a ditch," one gladiator mutters. Nods of agreement ripple through the ranks.

"What is the meaning of this cowardice?"

The ambassador storm onto the sand once more, his face dark with rage.

"Why are you standing there? There are dozens of you! Dozens!"

"Numbers mean nothing against fighters of that caliber," a gladiator shoots back.

choice("Continue", B2-Ch05b-Cancelled, v_current_scene = B2-Ch05b-Cancelled)


ID: B2-Ch05b-Cancelled
TEXT:

 "What caliber?" the ambassador shrieks, spitting with rage. "They are peasants! Unwashed vagabonds! If gold is not enough, name your price! I will grant you estates in the capital! You will never labor another day in your lives! I will raise your lineage to high rank so you never look upon a pit like this again! What do you desire? Name it! Only fight! Fight, damn you!"

The gladiators exchange uneasy glances, but no one reaches for a hilt. The fear in their eyes outweighs every promise of gold.

"What ails you?" the ambassador roars, veins throbbing against his neck. "Have you no ambition? No spine? What will it take to make you move? Tell me, you miserable excuses for men! What will it—"

A deep, mournful horn blast drowns out his voice.

A second horn answers from the northern ramparts, then a third from the harbour towers, ringing across the rooftops of Thilias in unison.

The crowd in the stands stiffens. Whispers turn to panicked murmurs. The locals recognize that call—a full alarm.

"Attention!" The announcer's voice booms through the amplification runes, trembling with panic. "All spectators will evacuate the coliseum in an orderly manner! The games are hereby cancelled! I repeat: the games are cancelled!"

The stands erupt into chaos. Thousands of citizens surge toward the stone vomitoria, shoving toward the daylight in a desperate rush to reach the streets.

The announcer leans over his rail toward our line on the sand.

"Gladiators," he calls down hurriedly. "Under the statutes of Thilias, a city-wide state of emergency conscripts all arena fighters into the royal garrison until the crisis passes. You are now under crown command."

choice(""Like hell, we will! That wasn't the deal!"", B2-Ch05b-Deal, v_current_scene = B2-Ch05b-Deal)
choice(""What is the emergency?"", B2-Ch05b-Emergency, v_current_scene = B2-Ch05b-Emergency)
choice(""What about the penalty round? Do we still have to do that too?"", B2-Ch05b-Penalty, v_current_scene = B2-Ch05b-Penalty)


ID: B2-Ch05b-Deal
TEXT:

 "Like hell, we will! That wasn't the deal!"

"There is no time for legal squabbling!" the announcer cries out, his voice cracking with terror. "Even if you refuse the draft, you have nowhere to run—"

A ferocious gale cuts him off mid-sentence.

The sudden downdraft hammers the arena floor with hurricane force, whipping sand into our eyes and forcing us to plant our boots to avoid being swept off our feet.

This wind... I have felt this gale once before.

"Half-lessathi," a deep, rumbling voice rolls down from above. "I have found you."

I look up toward the sky.

High above the open oval of the coliseum, Tyrath hovers on massive crimson wings. The king of dragons glares down at me with slit golden pupils burning with hatred.

"Gods preserve us..." Bruce whispers.

The announcer lets out a strangled shriek and tumbles backward off his podium. In the stands, the evacuation turns into a stampede as thousands of spectators shriek and scramble over stone benches to reach the exits.

The ambassador squeals in terror, hoists his embroidered robes, and sprints for the nearest iron gate.

"Did you imagine you could burrow underground forever, half-lessathi?" Tyrath's voice reverberates through the arena. "The moment you crawled into open air, your scent carried across the city. You have only prolonged the inevitable."

choice("Continue", B2-Ch05b-Seal, v_current_scene = B2-Ch05b-Seal)


